  "story": {
    "headline": "A New Study Points to Two Origins of Life on Earth by Tracing Early Chemical Reactions in Single-Celled Organisms",
    "summary": "The work challenges the assumption that all life descended from one free-living cell. Instead, it suggests that two microbial lineages, the bacteria and archaea, evolved independently from a primordial, nonliving ancestor",
    "publisher": "Rally News",
    "url": "https://rally.news/categories/world/?article=A%2BNew%2BStudy%2BPoints%2Bto%2BTwo%2BOrigins%2Bof%2BLife%2Bon%2BEarth%2Bby%2BTracing%2BEarly%2BChemical%2BReactions%2Bin%2BSingle-Celled%2BOrganisms"
  },
  "researchBrief": "The study published in Science Advances suggests that life on Earth may have originated twice, with bacteria and archaea evolving independently from a primordial ancestor. The research team traced early chemical reactions in single-celled organisms and found that the last universal common ancestor (LUCA) relied on metals in the environment for about half of its metabolic reactions. Over time, bacteria and archaea independently evolved different enzymes to replace these metal-catalyzed reactions. This finding challenges the long-held assumption that all life descended from one free-living cell. The study was corroborated by multiple sources, including Smithsonian Magazine, Phys.org, and ScienceAlert, which all highlighted the significance of the discovery. The key numbers and findings, such as the role of metals in early metabolism and the independent evolution of enzymes, were consistently reported across these sources.",
  "sources": [
    "https://www.smithsonianmag.com/science-nature/a-new-study-points-to-two-origins-of-life-on-earth-by-tracing-early-chemical-reactions-in-single-celled-organisms-180989260/",
    "https://www.sciencealert.com/radical-study-suggests-life-on-earth-arose-from-non-living-matter-twice",
    "https://www.science.org/content/article/our-last-common-ancestor-lived-4-2-billion-years-ago-perhaps-hundreds-millions-years",
    "https://www.newscientist.com/article/2468499-when-did-life-begin-on-earth-new-evidence-reveals-a-shocking-story/"
  ],
